ing baseline behavior untouched.\n\n3. **`_choose_setup_active(sel)`** — when choosing the opening Active: pick Mega Kangaskhan ex if it's a legal Active option; otherwise fall back to the existing static card-power ranking, but skip Yanma when any other Basic is available so Yanma stays on the Bench for the later Bench→Active Buzzing Boost trigger.\n\n4. **`_greedy_select` wiring** — a guarded branch that fires *only* on the setup-Active context, before the normal `SelectType` dispatch. Setup Bench placement and every other selection keep their prior behavior, so this is the smallest change that tests the hypothesis.\n\nBehavior delta: at opening Active selection, the agent now deterministically promotes Mega Kangaskhan ex when held (previously it ranked purely by `_card_power`, which does not necessarily favor Kangaskhan), and avoids promoting Yanma otherwise. Nothing outside opening Active placement changed.\n\n## Concerns for the reviewer\n\n- **\"Run Errand is usable\" is approximated by \"Kangaskhan is a legal Active at setup.\"** During setup we cannot inspect energy/hand to verify Run Errand is actually castable turn 1, so I gated on availability of the card as Active. If Run Errand has a non-trivial precondition the deck can't reliably meet, this preference could occasionally seat a 3-prize liability with no immediate payoff — worth confirming Run Errand is a no/low-cost draw attack usable early.\n- **Context-name assumption.** The setup-Active enum member name is inferred (`SETUP_ACTIVE_POKEMON`, confirmed only by the sibling `SETUP_BENCH_POKEMON` documented in POKEMON_RULES.md §15.7). I could not introspect `cg.api` in this workspace (no shell tools). If the real name differs, the branch is inert and the experiment shows *no effect* rather than a regression — please verify the name resolves so the mechanism is actually exercised.\n- **Bench placement intentionally unchanged.** \"Yanma on Bench\" is achieved solely by not promoting it to Active; existing bench-fill logic is preserved per the \"preserve existing choices outside opening Active/Bench placement\" clause.","ttft_ms":2465,"ttft_stream_ms":2146,"time_to_request_ms":173,"type":"result","duration_ms":144053,"uuid":"3d4f2a4a-439d-4eec-b8ab-e3c353c669dd"}
